# Blood assets

Run `python3 tools/assets/blood.py` from the repository root to download
the five Hell2025 decals and the complete Blood19/20/22 VAT datasets.
Use `python3 tools/assets/blood.py --convert` with Blender installed to
convert missing Blood20/22 FBX meshes to GLB.

The original `blood19.glb` and `blood_mesh.glb` are never overwritten.
An `assets/blood/manifest.json` is generated with SHA-256 hashes and
original VAT metadata. The desktop client uses downloaded PNG decals if
present and falls back to procedural red decals otherwise.

VAT datasets are 60 frames at 24 FPS. The EXR/lookup files retain their
original precision; importing the GLB alone does not reproduce VAT motion.

Source: https://github.com/livinamuk/Hell2025

**Review the upstream assets' copyright and licensing before redistributing
the models or textures.** The download utility does not grant a license.
